# §2. Ask 2 — IPW robust to both

Straightforwardly: **fit the §1 family *with* IPW weights.** IPW fixes selection; the corrected family fixes misspecification; they are orthogonal repairs and compose.

On your sharper point — §C shows failure depends on critical-point *type*, which is geometry, not \(\ell\), and you note that is my own caveat confirmed. It is, but it does not sink IPW, and here is the precise reason:

IPW does not require failure to be *caused* by \(\ell\). It requires the propensity to be **estimable from observables available for all 791 pairs**. Pixel lifetime is observed for every pair, including the 179 failures. So \(R(\ell_{\text{pix}})\) is estimable, and IPW is valid under

> **(CI)** exact lifetime \(\perp\) reconstruction failure, given pixel lifetime.

**That is the assumption to state and it is testable.** Among *successful* reconstructions, regress \(|\ell_{\text{exact}}-\ell_{\text{pix}}|\) on the type-check margin. If the margin predicts the discrepancy after conditioning on \(\ell_{\text{pix}}\), (CI) fails and IPW on \(\ell_{\text{pix}}\) alone is insufficient — you would then weight on \((\ell_{\text{pix}},\text{local Hessian conditioning})\), both observable pre-reconstruction.

